^SAMPLE = GSM8599465
!Sample_title = organoid, CRISPRi, DMSO, CROP-seq
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM8599465
!Sample_status = Public on Jun 26 2025
!Sample_submission_date = Oct 28 2024
!Sample_last_update_date = Jun 26 2025
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Stomach
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Stomach
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: TP53/APC KO Human Gastric Organoids
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: CRISPRi
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: DMSO
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = 10x gem_group: 1, 2, 3
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The organoids infected with the sgRNA library were dissociated into single cells, and the live cells were FACS sorted (BD FACS Aria2) to isolate them for single-cell RNA-seq
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Cells were prepared for single-cell RNA-seq using the 10X Chromium Controller and Chromium Single Cell 3' Library & Gel Bead Kit v2 (10x Genomics). From the final library, the sgRNA sequences are specifically amplified with PCR, as described before, with the following primers: 5'-AATGATACGGCGACCACCGAGATCTACAC-3' and  5’-CAAGCAGAAGACGGCATACGAGATCAGCCTCGGTCTCGTGGGCTCGGAGATGTGTATAAGAGACAGgtgttttgagactataaGtatcccttggagaaCCAcctTGTTG-3'. PCR cycling was performed according to the following protocol: (1) 95°C for 3 min, (2) 98°C for 15 s, then 70°C for 10 s (15 cycles) (3) 72 C for 1 min. The resulting sgRNA barcode library was purified via a 0.8X SPRI selection, and then further size was selected using BluePippin (Sage Science). sgRNA barcode libraries were sequenced as spike-ins alongside the parent RNA-seq libraries (5% spike-in) on a NovaSeq 6000, following the manufacturer’s recommendations.
!Sample_description = 10X Genomics
!Sample_description = filtered_feature_bc_matrix.h5
!Sample_description = cell_identities.csv
!Sample_description = matrix.mtx.gz
!Sample_description = features.tsv.gz
!Sample_description = barcodes.tsv.gz
!Sample_description = CRISPRi_reference_guide_barcode_library.xlsx
!Sample_data_processing = Cell Ranger (version 2.1.1, 10X Genomics) with default parameters was used to align reads and generate digital expression matrices from single-cell sequencing data. Cell sgRNA identity assignments were processed using custom Python scripts described previously. Cells with only one assigned sgRNA were retained for further analysis. Custom Python scripts described previously were used to analyze the digital expression matrices, including normalization, quality control, and filtering. To normalize for differences in sequencing capture and coverage across emulsion droplets, we rescaled all cells with the median number of total UMIs.  sgRNAs with lower than 10 cells were removed from the analysis. The expression of each gene was then z-normalized with respect to the mean and standard deviation of that gene in the control population.
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCh38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: 10X Genomics Cellranger output (filtered_feature_bc_matrix.h5)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: sgRNA identities for each cell
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: 10X Genomics Cellranger output (matrix.mtx.gz)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: 10X Genomics Cellranger output (features.tsv.gz)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: 10X Genomics Cellranger output (barcodes.tsv.gz)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: sgRNA library sequences and target genes
!Sample_platform_id = GPL24676
!Sample_contact_name = Jin,,Chen
!Sample_contact_laboratory = Jin Chen
!Sample_contact_institute = UT Southwestern Medical Center
!Sample_contact_address = 5323 Harry Hines Blvd
!Sample_contact_city = Dallas
!Sample_contact_state = TX
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 75390
!Sample_contact_country = USA
!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina NovaSeq 6000
!Sample_library_selection = cDNA
!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic single cell
!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN44479624
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX26524732
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE
!Sample_series_id = GSE280506
!Sample_data_row_count = 0
